"""
solver-prover.py -- local experiment, not a submitted artifact.

DERIVED WORK. Roughly half of this file (2,268 of 4,209 lines) is
`opnorm`, the SAIR Stage 2 reference solver shipped at
`examples/solo/demos/opnorm/` in the competition repository
(snapshot 2026-04-23), used and modified under Apache-2.0. Its
original docstring follows at the end of this header.

Over that: an embedded ETP implication bitmap used as a direction
oracle, a forced-singleton prover, a structured-magma refuter over
Z/m, and a proof-carrying completion prover for the true direction
(every `pv_*` name). The two bitmaps are binary blobs; competition
rules require any such payload to be disclosed in a submission note.

Removed from the build this was forked from: opnorm's LLM path, which
fired zero times across 200 problems, and six strategies hardcoded to
individual problem pairs, which could not fire on a graded set that
reuses no publicly available problem.

Measured 187/200 on a local sample set, NOT the graded set. See
../../docs/equational-prover.md and ../../docs/merge-experiment.md.

--- original opnorm docstring ---
opnorm — flagship reference mining solver (Solo track).

Strategy: 16 deterministic proof strategies (counterexample search on
Fin 2-7, singleton detection, library lookup, constancy lemmas, BFS
near-miss search, several calc-chain variants) followed by a single
structural-context LLM call. The LLM receives constancy / near-miss
analysis from the deterministic stages, so it usually only needs one
attempt when called.

Also distils Lean errors into structured feedback (error type,
expected vs actual types, specific fix hints) for the next LLM round
when the first attempt is rejected, instead of dumping raw stderr.

Reference snapshot dated 2026-04-23. See `examples/solo/TUTORIAL.md`
Walkthrough 3 for an annotated end-to-end run.
"""



